subject: feat(ui): visual fallback rule builder + markdown log explanation

User requested (2026-08-06): an easier way to create fallback rules than
the textarea, with auto-populating model pickers, ordered chains, and
retry counts (universal + per-model override). Also asked for the markdown
flush behavior to be explained clearly.

- ModelFallbacksSection now shows a rules TABLE (Target | Fallback Chain |
  Retries | Actions) with delete per row. Rules render with → chain arrows
  and per-model retry hints.
- New FallbackRuleModal: target picker (specific model via ModelSelectModal
  "Pick…" OR whole-provider id input), ordered fallback chain (add from
  the FULL model catalog picker, up/down reorder, remove), universal retries
  (1-10), and per-model retry overrides (1-10 or blank=inherit). Saves the
  advanced shape {target: {models, retries, perModelRetries}} which the
  backend (commit 8990a3b4) already consumes.
- Textarea power-user mode kept (toDraftText/parseDraftText) for advanced
  users.
- Markdown Log card now explicitly states the flush OVERWRITES the daily
  file with the latest 24h snapshot (not append), in both the card bullets
  and the interval field hint.

Refs: user request (session narrative, plans-and-prompts/SESSION-NARRATIVE.md);
backend retry support: commit 8990a3b4.

Part of: Smart Router & Fallback UX plan M3 (visual rule builder)

